# Allowlist. Exclude everything, then re-include only the site.
# With no build step, anything committed gets a public URL by default —
# a denylist would ship each new working note until someone remembered to add it.
*

# A directory needs both lines. These are gitignore patterns, so the bare `*`
# above matches at every depth: `!css/` re-includes the directory but `*` still
# excludes `css/style.css` on the way down. Without the `/**` line the site
# deploys as unstyled HTML with no scripts, fonts or images.
!*.html
!css/
!css/**
!js/
!js/**
!fonts/
!fonts/**
!img/
!img/**
!favicon.svg
!resume.pdf
!robots.txt
!sitemap.xml
!vercel.json

# Last match wins, so this re-excludes markdown the `/**` lines swept back in:
# img/README.md documents the .pix source contract and is not part of the site.
*.md

# stats.json is deliberately NOT re-included: it is served through a rewrite
# from the stats branch, and a deployed copy would override that rewrite.

# Prototypes, again. .gitignore already keeps them out of a git-triggered
# deploy, but `!*.html` above would sweep them back in on a `vercel` CLI
# deploy from a working tree, where the ignore file — not git — decides what
# uploads. Last match wins, so these belong at the end.
prototype-*.html
css/prototype-*.css
js/prototype-*.js
